  "prefLabel": "En 1302.14 Simple make-ready",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "En 1302.14 “Simple make-ready” means make-ready work where existing attachments in the communications space of a pole could be transferred without any reasonable expectation of a service outage or facility damage, and which does not require splicing of any existing communications attachment or relocation of any existing wireless attachment.\n\nSource. #13497, eff 12-1-22 (see Revision Note at chapter heading for En 1300)",
